    "https://careers.rpi.edu/jobs/director-sport-performance-and-wellness-troy-ny-new-york-united-states": {
      "title": "Director, Sport Performance and Wellness",
      "description": "Director, Sport Performance and Wellness - Troy, NY, New York, United States Director, Sport Performance and Wellness - Troy, NY, New York, United States Kiosk mode Director, Sport Performance and Wellness Troy, NY Athletics Business, Accounting and Finance Staff Full Time Job Summary: The Director, Sport Performance & Wellness is responsible for leading and managing the newly formed area of Sport Performance & Wellness in RPI Athletics. The Director will serve as the strategic oversight of data collection and integration to best enhance the safety and performance of our student-athletes. With direct oversight of the Strength & Conditioning unit, the Director will advise coaches on how to utilize this data for programming and work closely with Athletic Training to ensure training cycles support the wellbeing of student-athletes. This position will design and implement strength and conditioning sessions for our Division I hockey programs. Who we are: Founded in 1824, Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute (RPI) is the first technological research university in the United States. We bring creativity, science, and technology together to address society's greatest challenges. We cultivate exceptional problem-solvers by immersing them in a culture of rigorous inquiry, disciplined practice, and hands-on application. Our strategic plan, RPI Forward, charts a pioneering course for the next era of RPI. Explore the RPI Forward plan. ↗︎ Nestled on a beautiful 275-acre campus in upstate NY, RPI is home to five schools, 32 research centers, three makerspaces, an observatory, one of the world’s fastest supercomputers, and the IBM Quantum System One - the first university-based quantum computer in the world. With top notch employee health and retirement benefits, Rensselaer offers its full-time employees a generous paid time off program, tuition remission, and opportunities for career growth. Minimum Qualifications: 3 or more years as a head coach in the field of strength and conditioning or in a professional sport setting supporting the strength and conditioning development of athletes Demonstrated experience working with a collegiate ice hockey program and knowledge of the game of ice hockey. Strength and Conditioning Specialist Certification and/or NSCA Certification Relevant combinations of education, training and experience may be considered. Minimum Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Experience or certification in sport-related nutrition Knowledge of strength training, speed, agility, flexibility, and cardiovascular conditioning Knowledge of NCAA regulations and guidelines Demonstrated ability to motivate high-performing student-athletes Ability to initiate, develop and maintain contacts appropriate to developing an effective strength and conditioning program Knowledge of sport-related data including Catapult, Velocity-Based Training, and other wearables Ability to convey a clear and concise message while communicating, both verbally and in writing Ability to work effectively with a wide range of constituents Ability to read, design and enforce safety procedures Ability to foster a cooperative work environment Ability to work effectively under pressure and meet established goals and objectives Ability to make administrative/procedural decisions and judgments Representative Job Duties: Manage all aspects of sport-related data and wearable technology used across the athletic department. Ensure coaches, student-athletes, and staff (athletic training/strength and conditioning) are well trained in how to incorporate feedback from the data to design, adjust, and execute high-level training cycles that support student-athlete wellbeing. Present results of the data, as well as student-athlete performance and potential enhancements to programming, annually to the head coaches and director of athletics. Provide supervision, direction, and guidance to strength and conditioning staff, including recommendations related to best practices in athlete performance and recovery. Prepare guidelines for interns or others who are working in the strength and conditioning unit. Educate student-athletes on correct techniques of weightlifting, plyometrics, speed development drills, conditioning exercises, and agility movements. Design monthly sessions that educate strength and conditioning staff on industry trends. Ensure staff seek and complete necessary educational experiences to maintain certification(s). Assist with the coordination of wellness support for our Division I student-athletes in alignment with the NCAA Student-Athlete Core Guarantees, including education related to mental health, strength and conditioning, and nutrition. Collaborate with external partners to provide support in areas such as Sport Psychology or Sport Mental Performance. Work closely with Athletic Training staff to ensure an open line of communication between strength and conditioning staff in terms of rehabilitation and reinstatement of student-athletes in practice and competitions. Serve as a member of the Athletic Department Senior Staff, advising the strategic direction of the athletic department. Act as an advocate for student-athlete wellbeing and serve on campus committees supporting similar efforts. Maintain up-to-date manuals and SOPs for Strength and Conditioning, as well as Data Analytics or Use of Student-Athlete Performance Data. Perform other duties as assigned in support of the athletic department’s overall mission and operations. Shift: Primarily business hours; however, occasional evenings, weekends, and non-traditional hours are required based on student-athlete training needs, competition schedules, and departmental priorities. Travel: Travel is a significant component of the position (greater than 25%) and includes team travel, athletic events, professional development activities, and other department-related commitments. Driving: Incidental driving possible, but not required Starting Salary/Rate: Expected hiring range: $80,000 - $85,000 Pay transparency disclosure: The selected candidate’s salary will be determined based on factors that include the available budget, internal equity, and the final candidate’s qualifications, experience, education and other job-related credentials. This hiring range is provided as Rensselaer’s good faith estimate of the expected hiring range at the time of posting. Application instructions: Follow the on-screen prompts to create a brief online profile. Please be ready to upload your resume and cover letter. If you need assistance with the online application process, please contact careers@rpi.edu. Job Posted Date: Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Total Compensation and Benefits Information: Rensselaer’s Total Compensation Program is designed to provide stable pay growth, a comprehensive and affordable benefits package, and a comprehensive and affordable retiree medical and prescription plan. Our goal is to provide you and your family with a comprehensive health and welfare program as an umbrella of financial security and protection during your employment. For more information, please visit Benefits | Human Resources (rpi.edu) . Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute is committed to the cultivation of a community that is welcoming, inclusive, and above all values learning. We welcome candidates who bring a variety of perspectives to Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute's work and campus communities. Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation or gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or other characteristic protected by law. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 4258180c Last Name (required) 96cb3edf Email (required) a2f382d9 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Custodial Worker - Environmental Specialist Troy, NY Environmental & Site Services The Department of Environmental Services seeks applicants to fill its opening for several Cleaner openings. Public Safety Officer I Troy, NY Public Safety Office Entry level Public Safety opportunities available for service minded individuals interested in facilitating a safe and secure environment for the students, faculty, and staff who live, learn and work at Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute. Sergeant Troy, NY Public Safety Office The Public Safety Sergeant provides supervision of shift including responsibility for assigning and coordinating Officer duties, evaluation of daily patrol activity and reports, productivity reports, special events, conflict resolution, emergency response and law enforcement coordination. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert d95acd8d Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Athletics Business, Accounting and Finance Staff Athletics Business, Accounting and Finance Staff Employment Type Full Time Full Time Locations Troy, NY, New York, United States Troy, NY, New York, United States First Name (required) 5ac72827 Last Name (required) f37c835e Email (required) d22139dd Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
