    "https://careers.rpi.edu/jobs/public-safety-officer-i-troy-ny-new-york-united-states-26907ade-dee5-4c3d-a6e5-23807f9ca67b": {
      "title": "Public Safety Officer I",
      "description": "Public Safety Officer I - Troy, NY, New York, United States Public Safety Officer I - Troy, NY, New York, United States Kiosk mode Public Safety Officer I Troy, NY Public Safety Staff Full Time Add to favorites View favorites Who we are: Why Rensselaer? Nestled on a beautiful 275-acre campus in upstate NY, Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute is home to five schools, 32 research centers, three makerspaces, an observatory, one of the world’s fastest supercomputers, and the IBM Quantum System One - the first university-based quantum computer in the world. With top notch employee health and retirement benefits, Rensselaer offers its full-time employees a generous paid time off program, tuition remission, and opportunities for career growth. Job Summary: Entry level Public Safety opportunities available for service minded individuals interested in facilitating a safe and secure environment for the students, faculty, and staff who live, learn and work at Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute. The Public Safety Officer I is responsible for the detection and prevention of crime, for the protection of persons, property and the general maintenance of peace, order and security; duties include patrol, crowd control, traffic control and dispatching. Minimum Qualifications: Candidates will have, at least a some college credits after having completed high school or GED. College requirement not necessary for those with qualifying military service Must possess and maintain a valid US driver’s license Must have the ability to obtain and maintain a NYS Security Guard License CPR and AED certification must be completed within three months of hire All Public Safety Officer I incumbents must successfully complete Rensselaer's Field Officer Training Program within four (4) months of hire Must be available for flexible shift scheduling Note: Five (5) years of safety, security, law enforcement experience or other related experience may be substituted for college credits Relevant combinations of education, training and experience may be considered. Minimum Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Demonstrated ability to apply critical thinking skills Must possess the ability to assess a situation and apply appropriate conflict resolution techniques Ability to use crisis intervention techniques Ability to use relevant personal and/or mobile computing technology Must possess excellent verbal and written communication skills Requires ability to handle multiple emergency situations Requires excellent customer relations skills and the ability to deal effectively with a diverse population in an academic setting Preferred Knowledge, Skill, and Abilities • Knowledge of computerized emergency and data base systems Shift Public Safety: Various Shifts. All members of the Department of Public Safety must be available for flexible shift scheduling Including: 3rd shift 11:00 PM - 7:00 AM 2nd Shift 3:00 PM - 11:00 PM 1st Shift 7:00 AM - 3:00 PM Travel Local travel between campus locations only Driving Driving a Rensselaer vehicle for non-passenger use Salary Range/Rate Expected hiring range : Public Safety Officer I $20.25 Public Safety Officer II $22.55 Qualifications for Public Safety Officer II include: Officer II may require a higher educational standard, specialized certifications, or additional years of experience. At least five (5) years of combined safety, security, law enforcement, or related experience, which can substitute for college credits. Prior supervisory or leadership experience in a safety or security setting preferred. Advanced certifications in security or law enforcement practices. Pay transparency disclosure: The selected candidate’s salary will be determined based on factors that include the available budget, internal equity, and the final candidate’s qualifications, experience, education and other job-related credentials. This hiring range is provided as Rensselaer’s good faith estimate of the expected hiring range at the time of posting. For more details, and to apply Follow the on-screen prompts to create an application. Please be ready to upload your required documents. If you need assistance with the online application process, please contact careers@rpi.edu Applications Accepted Until Applications will be reviewed as they are received Total Compensation and Benefits Information Rensselaer’s Total Compensation Program is designed to provide stable pay growth, a comprehensive and affordable benefits package, and a comprehensive and affordable retiree medical and prescription plan. Rensselaer is recognized locally and nationally for the depth and breadth of its compensation and benefits program. Our goal is to provide you and your family with a comprehensive health and welfare program as an umbrella of financial security and protection during your employment. For more information, please visit Benefits | Human Resources (rpi.edu) . Rensselaer is committed to the cultivation of a community that is welcoming, inclusive, and above all values learning. We welcome candidates who bring a variety of perspectives to Rensselaer’s work and campus communities. RPI is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation or gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or other characteristic protected by law. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) cedb8eee Last Name (required) 74c1e4a6 Email (required) cfe03121 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Custodial Worker - Environmental Specialist Troy, NY Environmental & Site Services The Department of Environmental Services seeks applicants to fill its opening for several Cleaner openings. Sergeant Troy, NY Public Safety Office The Public Safety Sergeant provides supervision of shift including responsibility for assigning and coordinating Officer duties, evaluation of daily patrol activity and reports, productivity reports, special events, conflict resolution, emergency response and law enforcement coordination. Pre-College Advisor Troy, NY Pipeline Initiatives The Pre-College Advisor will serve as an academic advisor for college readiness and as a central resource for all RPI STEP students in grades 7-12. The Advisor will advise and counsel RPI STEP students on academic course requirements and selection to graduate high school and pursue college and career in STEM fields, including advising them on the college application process and choosing the right fit college The Advisor will report to the STEP Director and work with the STEP staff and guidance counselors at partner schools to monitor RPI STEP students’ academic performance in the STEM fields. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 095fafdd Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Public Safety Staff Public Safety Staff Employment Type Full Time Full Time Locations Troy, NY, New York, United States Troy, NY, New York, United States First Name (required) fbac84d1 Last Name (required) 2204bfb9 Email (required) ba05abe3 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
