    "https://careers.rpi.edu/jobs/executive-housekeeper-part-time-troy-ny-new-york-united-states": {
      "title": "Executive Housekeeper (Part Time)",
      "description": "Executive Housekeeper (Part Time) - Troy, NY, New York, United States Executive Housekeeper (Part Time) - Troy, NY, New York, United States Kiosk mode Executive Housekeeper (Part Time) Troy, NY Staff Trades, Service, and Maintenance Part Time Add to favorites View favorites Who we are Why Rensselaer? Nestled on a beautiful 275-acre campus in upstate NY, Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute is home to five schools, 32 research centers, three makerspaces, an observatory, one of the world’s fastest supercomputers, and the IBM Quantum System One - the first university-based quantum computer in the world. With top notch employee health and retirement benefits, Rensselaer offers its full-time employees a generous paid time off program, tuition remission, and opportunities for career growth. Job Summary This is a part-time position. The executive housekeeper performs a variety of housekeeping duties for the residence of the President of Rensselaer in accordance with established standards and procedures. The executive housekeeper will periodically inventory supplies and equipment; investigate new and improved cleaning instruments and make recommendations to the House manager. Minimum Qualifications • HS Diploma or equivalent preferred • Demonstrated stable work history is required, along with • One year experience in professional/residential cleaning services including training to operate cleaning machines Relevant combinations of education, training and experience may be considered. Preferred Qualifications Valid US driver license preferred Representative Duties Cleans floors, washes windows, cleans, dusts, and polishes indoor surfaces (door panels, and sills, walls, etc.) Cleans, sanitizes, and replenishes bathrooms. Does dishes, puts away groceries, takes out the trash. Does laundry and provides cleaning services during special events held at President’s residence. Minimum Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities • Ability to follow instructions, use cleaning materials manuals, operate power equipment, and handle sanitizing agents. • Ability to ensure privacy, confidentiality and discretion in all interactions at the President’s residence • Ability to work in a team environment and communicate with other employees, faculty, and students in campus community • Ability to read, write, and perform basic arithmetic Shift Tuesdays, Wednesdays, and Thursdays 9:00 a.m. through 3:00 p.m Travel Local travel between campus locations only Driving Preferred: Driving a personal vehicle for non-passenger use Starting Salary/Rate Expected hiring range: $20.00 - $22.15 Pay transparency disclosure: The selected candidate’s salary will be determined based on factors that include the available budget, internal equity, and the final candidate’s qualifications, experience, education and other job-related credentials. This hiring range is provided as Rensselaer’s good faith estimate of the expected hiring range at the time of posting. Application instructions Follow the on-screen prompts to create a brief online profile. Please be ready to upload your resume and cover letter. If you need assistance with the online application process, please contact careers@rpi.edu. Job Posted Date Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Total Compensation and Benefits Information Rensselaer’s Total Compensation Program is designed to provide stable pay growth, a comprehensive and affordable benefits package, and a comprehensive and affordable retiree medical and prescription plan. Rensselaer is recognized locally and nationally for the depth and breadth of its compensation and benefits program. Our goal is to provide you and your family with a comprehensive health and welfare program as an umbrella of financial security and protection during your employment. For more information, please visit Benefits | Human Resources (rpi.edu) . Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute is committed to the cultivation of a community that is welcoming, inclusive, and above all values learning. We welcome candidates who bring a variety of perspectives to Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute's work and campus communities. Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation or gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or other characteristic protected by law. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 4e0288ef Last Name (required) 7365ede0 Email (required) 6a1e2fea Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Custodial Worker - Environmental Specialist Troy, NY Environmental & Site Services The Department of Environmental Services seeks applicants to fill its opening for several Cleaner openings. Public Safety Officer I Troy, NY Public Safety Office Entry level Public Safety opportunities available for service minded individuals interested in facilitating a safe and secure environment for the students, faculty, and staff who live, learn and work at Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute. Sergeant Troy, NY Public Safety Office The Public Safety Sergeant provides supervision of shift including responsibility for assigning and coordinating Officer duties, evaluation of daily patrol activity and reports, productivity reports, special events, conflict resolution, emergency response and law enforcement coordination. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 98063ce3 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Staff Trades, Service, and Maintenance Staff Trades, Service, and Maintenance Employment Type Part Time Part Time Locations Troy, NY, New York, United States Troy, NY, New York, United States First Name (required) aacb90