    "https://careers.rpi.edu/jobs/pre-college-advisor-troy-ny-new-york-united-states": {
      "title": "Pre-College Advisor",
      "description": "Pre-College Advisor - Troy, NY, New York, United States Pre-College Advisor - Troy, NY, New York, United States Kiosk mode Pre-College Advisor Troy, NY CFHE Staff Student Affairs Professionals Full Time Add to favorites View favorites Job Summary: The Pre-College Advisor will serve as an academic advisor for college readiness and as a central resource for all RPI STEP students in grades 7-12. The Advisor will advise and counsel RPI STEP students on academic course requirements and selection to graduate high school and pursue college and career in STEM fields, including advising them on the college application process and choosing the right fit college The Advisor will report to the STEP Director and work with the STEP staff and guidance counselors at partner schools to monitor RPI STEP students’ academic performance in the STEM fields. Who we are: Founded in 1824, Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute (RPI) is the first technological research university in the United States. We bring creativity, science, and technology together to address society's greatest challenges. We cultivate exceptional problem-solvers by immersing them in a culture of rigorous inquiry, disciplined practice, and hands-on application. Our strategic plan, RPI Forward, charts a pioneering course for the next era of RPI. Explore the RPI Forward plan. ↗︎ Nestled on a beautiful 275-acre campus in upstate NY, RPI is home to five schools, 32 research centers, three makerspaces, an observatory, one of the world’s fastest supercomputers, and the IBM Quantum System One - the first university-based quantum computer in the world. With top notch employee health and retirement benefits, RPI offers its full-time employees a generous paid time off program, tuition remission, and opportunities for career growth. Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's Degree in relevant field 2 or more years experience in academic advising, student services, student affairs, career development or related field Applicants must meet stated minimum education and experience requirements. Minimum Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Exceptional interpersonal skills with the ability to influence and build working relationships with a culturally diverse population at all levels across the Institute Ability to create a welcoming environment that is inclusive of students from all backgrounds Ability to efficiently multi task, work under pressure, handle frequent interruptions and meet deadlines Proficiency in MS Office Suite software applications Strong organizational and time management skills with emphasis on accuracy and attention to detail in a complex organizational environment Ability to work independently and contribute to a team environment Ability to work effectively under pressure and meet established goals and objectives Ability to anticipate and solve problems Ability to initiate projects and function as a self-starter Ability to maintain a high degree of confidentiality and apply FERPA regulations Representative Job Duties: Catalog and maintain application requirements and admissions trends for STEM colleges/degrees and requirements for various STEM careers. Work with students and their parents to create individualized academic plans and benchmarks, and review and revise annually throughout middle and high school. Develop, implement, and maintain advising templates to aid students in choosing a career and the college application process. Oversee tutoring/mentoring programs encompassing best practices to assist students with their academics in line with Next Gen Science and Math Standards. Design and execute annual training for tutors/mentors in compliance with Institute requirements and consistent with the guidelines set forth by NYSED and governing regulatory bodies for working with minor children. Provide oversight and guidance to tutors/mentors working on campus, virtually and in partner school locations. Assist in participant recruitment and retention for RPI STEP and serve as a primary point of contact for students and their parents to ensure STEP-related academic support questions are answered and concerns are resolved. Administer the RPI STEP Path-to-Success and College Boot Camp programs for Junior and Senior students and families, in collaboration with Institute departments. Assist in the coordination and supervision of college visit programs. Identify key Institute events, lectures, open houses, etc., appropriate for STEP participants and families to attend, and coordinate participation when possible. Collaborate with STEP coordinators in partner schools to ensure that participants are taking advantage of available programs and resources, including social and emotional support programs. Coordinate with the RPI STEP staff to guide students’ personal and academic success, including in RPI STEP project-based learning courses that promote inquiry-based learning. Work with the Director ensure that all data and reporting of academic performance is collected, monitored and reported accurately to NYSED. Biannually certify that the students are eligible to continue in the program. Shift: Business Hours with weekends or evenings occasionally required Travel: Occasional overnight travel may be required (10% or less) Driving: Driving a personal vehicle for non-passenger use Starting Salary/Rate: Expected hiring range: $62,354 Pay transparency disclosure: The selected candidate’s salary will be determined based on factors that include the available budget, internal equity, and the final candidate’s qualifications, experience, education and other job-related credentials. This hiring range is provided as Rensselaer’s good faith estimate of the expected hiring range at the time of posting. Application instructions: Follow the on-screen prompts to create a brief online profile. Please be ready to upload your resume and cover letter. If you need assistance with the online application process, please contact careers@rpi.edu. Job Posted Date: Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Total Compensation and Benefits Information: RPI's Total Compensation Program is designed to provide stable pay growth, a comprehensive and affordable benefits package, and a comprehensive and affordable retiree medical and prescription plan. Our goal is to provide you and your family with a comprehensive health and welfare program as an umbrella of financial security and protection during your employment. For more information, please visit Benefits | Human Resources (rpi.edu) . Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute is committed to the cultivation of a community that is welcoming, inclusive, and above all values learning. We welcome candidates who bring a variety of perspectives to Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute's work and campus communities. Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation or gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or other characteristic protected by law. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 4531b0f6 Last Name (required) a03b0cbb Email (required) 691844ca Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Custodial Worker - Environmental Specialist Troy, NY Environmental & Site Services The Department of Environmental Services seeks applicants to fill its opening for several Cleaner openings. Public Safety Officer I Troy, NY Public Safety Office Entry level Public Safety opportunities available for service minded individuals interested in facilitating a safe and secure environment for the students, faculty, and staff who live, learn and work at Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute. Sergeant Troy, NY Public Safety Office The Public Safety Sergeant provides supervision of shift including responsibility for assigning and coordinating Officer duties, evaluation of daily patrol activity and reports, productivity reports, special events, conflict resolution, emergency response and law enforcement coordination. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 4f26c8ce Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories CFHE Staff Student Affairs Professionals CFHE Staff Student Affairs Professionals Employment Type Full Time Full Time Locations Troy, NY, New York, United States Troy, NY, New York, United States First Name (required) 362b3f59 Last Name (required) 5e17c6df Email (required) 62e2744a Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
