    "https://careers.rpi.edu/jobs/associate-director-campus-engagement-visit-experience-troy-ny-new-york-united-states": {
      "title": "Associate Director, Campus Engagement & Visit Experience",
      "description": "Associate Director, Campus Engagement & Visit Experience - Troy, NY, New York, United States Associate Director, Campus Engagement & Visit Experience - Troy, NY, New York, United States Kiosk mode Associate Director, Campus Engagement & Visit Experience Troy, NY Human Resources Staff Student Services and Academic Support Full Time Add to favorites View favorites Job Summary: The Associate Director, Campus Engagement and Visit Experience leads the full campus visit and yield event operation, the point at which admitted students most often decide to enroll. The position brings tours, information sessions, open houses, and yield events under a single owner, with attention to the quality and consistency of the visitor experience and to the data that links visits to deposits. Reporting to the Assistant Vice Provost for Undergraduate Admissions, the Associate Director leads the campus engagement strategy and supervises the staff who support it, with the goal of raising yield among admitted students. Who we are: Founded in 1824, Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute (RPI) is the first technological research university in the United States. We bring creativity, science, and technology together to address society's greatest challenges. We cultivate exceptional problem-solvers by immersing them in a culture of rigorous inquiry, disciplined practice, and hands-on application. Our strategic plan, RPI Forward, charts a pioneering course for the next era of RPI. Explore the RPI Forward plan. ↗︎ Nestled on a beautiful 275-acre campus in upstate NY, RPI is home to five schools, 32 research centers, three makerspaces, an observatory, one of the world’s fastest supercomputers, and the IBM Quantum System One - the first university-based quantum computer in the world. With top notch employee health and retirement benefits, Rensselaer offers its full-time employees a generous paid time off program, tuition remission, and opportunities for career growth. Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s Degree Five (5) or more years of progressively responsible experience in admissions, enrollment management, campus visit programs, event management, student services, or a related field, including: A minimum of two (2) years of supervisory experience. Demonstrated experience planning and executing large-scale events, campus visit programs, or recruitment initiatives. Experience managing multiple projects simultaneously while meeting deadlines in a fast-paced environment. Experience using customer relationship management (CRM) systems, event management platforms, and data reporting tools. Experience managing budgets, contracts, vendors, and event logistics. Relevant combinations of education, training and experience may be considered. Preferred Qualification: Valid driver’s license and a pattern of responsibility consistent with safe and responsible driving practices. Minimum Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Knowledge of undergraduate admissions, recruitment, enrollment management, and student engagement practices. Knowledge of current trends and best practices in campus visits, enrollment marketing, student engagement, and event management. Ability to develop and implement strategic campus engagement and yield initiatives aligned with institutional enrollment goals. Ability to analyze data, identify trends, and make data-informed recommendations to improve visitor and enrollment outcomes. Strong leadership, coaching, and staff development skills. Excellent organizational and project management skills with the ability to manage multiple priorities and complex logistics. Strong interpersonal, written, and verbal communication skills with the ability to build collaborative relationships across campus. Ability to establish collaborative partnerships with faculty, staff, students, and external vendors. Strong presentation and public speaking skills. Proficiency with CRM systems, event management software, Microsoft Office Suite, and data visualization and reporting tools. Ability to exercise sound judgment, solve problems creatively, and maintain attention to detail while delivering a high-quality visitor experience. Representative Job Duties: Plan and direct the full campus visit program, including daily visits, tours, information sessions, and group programs. Design and lead yield events for admitted students, on campus and in regional settings. Set and maintain standards for the quality and consistency of the visitor experience. Track and analyze the data that connects visits and events to applications, deposits, and enrollment, and adjust the program accordingly. Coordinate with recruitment, operations, marketing, and campus partners to deliver a seamless visitor experience. Manage the visit and event budget and the related vendor and logistics arrangements. Shift: Business Hours with weekends or evenings occasionally required Travel: Occasional overnight travel may be required(10% or less) Driving: Driving a personal vehicle for non-passenger use preferred Starting Salary/Rate: Expected hiring range: $71,500 - $89,000 Pay transparency disclosure: The selected candidate’s salary will be determined based on factors that include the available budget, internal equity, and the final candidate’s qualifications, experience, education and other job-related credentials. This hiring range is provided as Rensselaer’s good faith estimate of the expected hiring range at the time of posting. Application instructions: Follow the on-screen prompts to create a brief online profile. Please be ready to upload your resume and cover letter. If you need assistance with the online application process, please contact careers@rpi.edu. Job Posted Date: Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Total Compensation and Benefits Information: Rensselaer’s Total Compensation Program is designed to provide stable pay growth, a comprehensive and affordable benefits package, and a comprehensive and affordable retiree medical and prescription plan. Our goal is to provide you and your family with a comprehensive health and welfare program as an umbrella of financial security and protection during your employment. For more information, please visit Benefits | Human Resources (rpi.edu) . Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute is committed to the cultivation of a community that is welcoming, inclusive, and above all values learning. We welcome candidates who bring a variety of perspectives to Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute's work and campus communities. Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation or gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or other characteristic protected by law. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 12eb9b31 Last Name (required) a45c28d9 Email (required) 31118a95 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Custodial Worker - Environmental Specialist Troy, NY Environmental & Site Services The Department of Environmental Services seeks applicants to fill its opening for several Cleaner openings. Public Safety Officer I Troy, NY Public Safety Office Entry level Public Safety opportunities available for service minded individuals interested in facilitating a safe and secure environment for the students, faculty, and staff who live, learn and work at Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute. Sergeant Troy, NY Public Safety Office The Public Safety Sergeant provides supervision of shift including responsibility for assigning and coordinating Officer duties, evaluation of daily patrol activity and reports, productivity reports, special events, conflict resolution, emergency response and law enforcement coordination. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert b09628e2 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Human Resources Staff Student Services and Academic Support Human Resources Staff Student Services and Academic Support Employment Type Full Time Full Time Locations Troy, NY, New York, United States Troy, NY, New York, United States First Name (required) 1cc2a725 Last Name (required) 12dde603 Email (required) fcb43527 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
    },
    "https://careers.rpi.edu/jobs/assistant-director-athletic-facilities-equipment-operations-troy-ny-new-york-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, Athletic Facilities, Equipment & Operations",
      "description": "Assistant Director, Athletic Facilities, Equipment & Operations - Troy, NY, New York, United States Assistant Director, Athletic Facilities, Equipment & Operations - Troy, NY, New York, United States Kiosk mode Assistant Director, Athletic Facilities, Equipment & Operations Troy, NY Athletics Staff Full Time Add to favorites View favorites Job Summary: The Assistant Director, Athletic Facilities, Equipment & Operations will oversee the day-to-day operations of specified athletic facilities, including scheduling, maintenance, and custodial services. The assistant director directly supervises athletic facilities and student staff and is the liaison for ROTC, athletic contests, and internal/external events. The assistant director oversees inventory, ordering within an assigned sports budget, issuance, laundry service, and repair for athletic equipment. Who we are: Founded in 1824, Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute (RPI) is the first technological research university in the United States. We bring creativity, science, and technology together to address society's greatest challenges. We cultivate exceptional problem-solvers by immersing them in a culture of rigorous inquiry, disciplined practice, and hands-on application. Our strategic plan, RPI Forward, charts a pioneering course for the next era of RPI. Explore the RPI Forward plan. ↗︎ Nestled on a beautiful 275-acre campus in upstate NY, RPI is home to five schools, 32 research centers, three makerspaces, an observatory, one of the world’s fastest supercomputers, and the IBM Quantum System One - the first university-based quantum computer in the world. With top notch employee health and retirement benefits, RPI offers its full-time employees a generous paid time off program, tuition remission, and opportunities for career growth. Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in a related field. Three or more years of directly related experience in athletic equipment and facilities. One to two years of aquatic-related experience. Supervisory experience. Valid U.S. driver’s license. Certified Pool Operator (CPO) certification. A relevant combination of education, directly related experience and training may be substituted for a degree. Preferred Qualifications: Professional equipment manager certification Minimum Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Knowledge of NCAA regulations and guidelines Ability to provide day-to-day direction to staff and lead projects Knowledge of athletic terminology and equipment Thorough knowledge of the methods, tools, equipment, and materials normally used in maintenance Ability to work under strict time constraints Basic computer skills including Microsoft and job specific software Ability to work independently and as part of a team Excellent customer service skills Ability to communicate effectively Must have the ability to work flexible hours which may include, evenings, nights, weekends and holidays Demonstrated commitment to diversity and inclusion Representative Job Duties: Oversee the day-to-day operation of the pool, including scheduling, staffing, and equipment maintenance. Maintain an accurate budget projection of maintenance requests, projected annual maintenance needs, and chemicals required to support the daily operation of the pool. Order, test, and maintain chemical levels as required by the Board of Health. Vacuum the pool and clean the pool deck area routinely. Monitor and repair safety equipment, diving boards, and timing system. Coordinate yearly Board of Health inspections, complete Pool Permit applications, and keep daily records for the Rensselaer County Board of Health. Schedule, supervise, and train athletic facilities positions and student staff to support equipment and facility operations. Work with Manager to schedule the facilities, card access schedule, and field light schedule. Provide input on facilities master plan, capital projects, and performance plans. Prepare schedule to ensure appropriate distribution of work and ensure coverage for vacations, sick leave and/or personal leave. Provide recommendations for hiring, promotions, commendations, discipline, and termination. Prepare and submit personnel timesheets. Supervise and serve as a liaison for Administrative Associates within ROTC. Provide supervision, direction and guidance to assigned staff. Provide effective coaching/counseling to staff, completes performance evaluations, and participates in hiring process. Serve as liaison to ROTC commanding officers. Cross collaborate with the Office of the Provost to ensure streamlined communication in support of ROTC programming and recruitment. Oversee all aspects of equipment including issue, sizing, protective equipment maintenance, and uniforms. Arrange for equipment and uniform repair including sending out equipment for reconditioning and discarding unsafe equipment. Provide feedback to coaches regarding equipment usage, repair, and ordering. Maintain smooth flow of laundry providing support for each team and student athletes. Supervise and coordinate the set up, execution, and tear down for events. Assist coaches with set ups for practices and intercollegiate contests. Monitor the athletic facilities for all daily on-site activities and report any problems, issues or damages. Monitor and ensure adequate supply of equipment for intramurals and general use. Provide assistance to outside constituencies utilizing the facilities and event spectators. Welcome and escort visiting teams and officials to locker rooms. Assist physical facilities to insure the efficiency, functionality, appearance and safety of the facilities. Oversee all custodial needs for the buildings; perform custodial work as needed, maintain adequate supplies. Observes all operating and safety regulations necessary for the protection of equipment, property and personnel. Perform other duties as requested or assigned. Shift: Non-Standard Work Hours: This position may require work outside of standard business hours, including evenings, weekends, and holidays, based on departmental operations, events, and business needs. Travel: Local travel between campus locations only Driving: Incidental driving possible, but not required Starting Salary/Rate: Expected hiring range: $63,000- $66,300 Pay transparency disclosure: The selected candidate’s salary will be determined based on factors that include the available budget, internal equity, and the final candidate’s qualifications, experience, education and other job-related credentials. This hiring range is provided as RPI's good faith estimate of the expected hiring range at the time of posting. Application instructions: Follow the on-screen prompts to create a brief online profile. Please be ready to upload your resume and cover letter. If you need assistance with the online application process, please contact careers@rpi.edu. Job Posted Date: Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Total Compensation and Benefits Information: RPI's Total Compensation Program is designed to provide stable pay growth, a comprehensive and affordable benefits package, and a comprehensive and affordable retiree medical and prescription plan. Our goal is to provide you and your family with a comprehensive health and welfare program as an umbrella of financial security and protection during your employment. For more information, please visit Benefits | Human Resources (rpi.edu) . Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute is committed to the cultivation of a community that is welcoming, inclusive, and above all values learning. We welcome candidates who bring a variety of perspectives to Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute's work and campus communities. Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation or gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or other characteristic protected by law. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) c2cbff83 Last Name (required) 2d920902 Email (required) 6e0e75a5 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Custodial Worker - Environmental Specialist Troy, NY Environmental & Site Services The Department of Environmental Services seeks applicants to fill its opening for several Cleaner openings. Public Safety Officer I Troy, NY Public Safety Office Entry level Public Safety opportunities available for service minded individuals interested in facilitating a safe and secure environment for the students, faculty, and staff who live, learn and work at Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute. Sergeant Troy, NY Public Safety Office The Public Safety Sergeant provides supervision of shift including responsibility for assigning and coordinating Officer duties, evaluation of daily patrol activity and reports, productivity reports, special events, conflict resolution, emergency response and law enforcement coordination. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 7c6032a9 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Athletics Staff Athletics Staff Employment Type Full Time Full Time Locations Troy, NY, New York, United States Troy, NY, New York, United States First Name (required) 8c378651 Last Name (required) 3928ffcf Email (required) 995f3071 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
    },
    "https://careers.rpi.edu/jobs/groundskeeper-or-groundskeeper-sr-troy-ny-new-york-united-states": {
      "title": "Groundskeeper or Groundskeeper, Sr.",
      "description": "Groundskeeper or Groundskeeper, Sr. - Troy, NY, New York, United States Groundskeeper or Groundskeeper, Sr. - Troy, NY, New York, United States Kiosk mode Groundskeeper or Groundskeeper, Sr. Troy, NY Staff Trades, Service, and Maintenance Full Time Add to favorites View favorites Job Summary: The Groundskeeper performs grounds and landscape duties, snow removal and equipment operations associated with the maintenance of the campus grounds and athletic fields and support all campus wide events. Who we are: Founded in 1824, Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute (RPI) is the first technological research university in the United States. We bring creativity, science, and technology together to address society's greatest challenges. We cultivate exceptional problem-solvers by immersing them in a culture of rigorous inquiry, disciplined practice, and hands-on application. Our strategic plan, RPI Forward, charts a pioneering course for the next era of RPI. Explore the RPI Forward plan. ↗︎ Nestled on a beautiful 275-acre campus in upstate NY, RPI is home to five schools, 32 research centers, three makerspaces, an observatory, one of the world’s fastest supercomputers, and the IBM Quantum System One - the first university-based quantum computer in the world. With top notch employee health and retirement benefits, Rensselaer offers its full-time employees a generous paid time off program, tuition remission, and opportunities for career growth. Minimum Qualifications: All candidates must have a High school diploma or equivalent One (1) year of experience in landscape maintenance including operation of grounds related equipment Valid US driver's license As a Sr. Groundskeeper, candidates must also have Three (3) year experience in landscape maintenance including operation of grounds related equipment Relevant combinations of education, training and experience will be considered. Minimum Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Ability to operate hand power equipment and grounds related maintenance equipment Ability to read, write and perform simple arithmetic Basic computer skills including Microsoft and job specific software Ability to work independently and as part of a team Excellent customer service skills Ability to communicate effectively Must have the ability to work flexible hours which may include, evenings, nights, weekends and holidays Representative Job Duties: Perform all tasks necessary for routine maintenance of athletic fields and campus landscapes/projects in accordance with Rensselaer’s seasonal grounds maintenance program. Monitor campus grounds for trash/debris and empty/clean external trash areas. Perform proper planting techniques for trees, shrubs, groundcovers, bulbs, perennials and annuals. Perform proper bed maintenance techniques such as weeding, edging, mulching, plant removal/replacement, seasonal cleanup, pruning and dead-heading. Inspect, maintain and operate grounds and field related power equipment at proper working and safety standards. Clean equipment daily or at the end of each use . Report and document any needed repairs of equipment. Provide support for campus functions and events, including event preparation, setup and breakdown, litter control and site restoration. Provide support for athletic field operations and campus moves as required. Maintain water requirements for plant material and turf areas. Utilize manual irrigation when conditions warrant. Perform snow removal functions in accordance with the Institute snow removal plan. Respond to and be available for weather related emergencies as necessary to maintain safe transportation through campus. Operate, maintain and inspect all snow removal equipment in accordance with Institute’s standards. Comply with standing instructions provided by operating manuals, safety rules and regulations for personal protection and safety and the safety of others. Report instances of vandalism/theft of Institute property immediately to Supervisor or Public Safety. Maintain work and storage areas in a clean, organized and safe condition. Perform other duties as assigned. Shift: Business hours with occasional early mornings, evenings, weekends, holidays, and emergency response hours required based on operational needs, seasonal activities, campus events, and weather-related conditions. This position may require flexibility during peak grounds maintenance periods and snow removal operations. Travel: Local travel between Rensselaer campus locations and athletic facilities is required. Travel is limited to Institute-owned properties and nearby campus areas as needed to perform grounds maintenance, event support, athletic field preparation, and snow removal activities. Driving: Requires operation of Rensselaer vehicles and grounds maintenance equipment for non-passenger use. A valid U.S. driver’s license is required. Employees may operate campus vehicles, utility carts, trailers, and grounds-related equipment in support of daily operations, campus events, and emergency response activities. Must maintain a safe driving record in accordance with Institute policies. Starting Salary/Rate: Expected hiring range: Groundskeeper: $18.00 + An additional $0.20 per hour will be paid for each year of documented and related experience as approved by the hiring team, up to $19.50 per hour Sr. Groundskeeper: $19.50 - $22.50 per hour Pay transparency disclosure: The selected candidate’s salary will be determined based on factors that include the available budget, internal equity, and the final candidate’s qualifications, experience, education and other job-related credentials. This hiring range is provided as Rensselaer’s good faith estimate of the expected hiring range at the time of posting. Application instructions: Follow the on-screen prompts to create a brief online profile. Please be ready to upload your resume and cover letter. If you need assistance with the online application process, please contact careers@rpi.edu. Job Posted Date: Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Total Compensation and Benefits Information: Rensselaer’s Total Compensation Program is designed to provide stable pay growth, a comprehensive and affordable benefits package, and a comprehensive and affordable retiree medical and prescription plan. Our goal is to provide you and your family with a comprehensive health and welfare program as an umbrella of financial security and protection during your employment. For more information, please visit Benefits | Human Resources (rpi.edu) . Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute is committed to the cultivation of a community that is welcoming, inclusive, and above all values learning. We welcome candidates who bring a variety of perspectives to Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute's work and campus communities. Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation or gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or other characteristic protected by law. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) e4620206 Last Name (required) e431c40d Email (required) b688c300 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Custodial Worker - Environmental Specialist Troy, NY Environmental & Site Services The Department of Environmental Services seeks applicants to fill its opening for several Cleaner openings. Public Safety Officer I Troy, NY Public Safety Office Entry level Public Safety opportunities available for service minded individuals interested in facilitating a safe and secure environment for the students, faculty, and staff who live, learn and work at Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute. Sergeant Troy, NY Public Safety Office The Public Safety Sergeant provides supervision of shift including responsibility for assigning and coordinating Officer duties, evaluation of daily patrol activity and reports, productivity reports, special events, conflict resolution, emergency response and law enforcement coordination. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 11460328 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Staff Trades, Service, and Maintenance Staff Trades, Service, and Maintenance Employment Type Full Time Full Time Locations Troy, NY, New York, United States Troy, NY, New York, United States First Name (required) 456ffeff Last Name (required) 0da60d08 Email (required) 3d3f4f6b Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
