    "https://careers.rpi.edu/jobs/counselor-ii-10-months-troy-ny-new-york-united-states": {
      "title": "Counselor II (10-months)",
      "description": "Counselor II (10-months) - Troy, NY, New York, United States Counselor II (10-months) - Troy, NY, New York, United States Kiosk mode Counselor II (10-months) Troy, NY CFHE Health Services Staff Full Time Add to favorites View favorites Job Summary: The Counselor II will facilitate the normal developmental process of Rensselaer students and assist students whose normal developmental process is being impeded by adjustment problems and other disorders. The Counselor will work with students individually and in groups, as well as proactively work with the Rensselaer Community to create an environment that will allow students to maximize their personal growth. This position will also develop and implement mental health prevention and education programs. NOTE: This is a 10-month role with a scheduled work period of August 1 through May 31 of the following year. The position will enter the non-work period beginning June 1, extending through July 31. This role is eligible for year-round benefits. Who we are: Founded in 1824, Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute (RPI) is the first technological research university in the United States. We bring creativity, science, and technology together to address society's greatest challenges. We cultivate exceptional problem-solvers by immersing them in a culture of rigorous inquiry, disciplined practice, and hands-on application. Our strategic plan, RPI Forward, charts a pioneering course for the next era of RPI. Explore the RPI Forward plan. ↗︎ Nestled on a beautiful 275-acre campus in upstate NY, RPI is home to five schools, 32 research centers, three makerspaces, an observatory, one of the world’s fastest supercomputers, and the IBM Quantum System One - the first university-based quantum computer in the world. With top notch employee health and retirement benefits, Rensselaer offers its full-time employees a generous paid time off program, tuition remission, and opportunities for career growth. Minimum Qualifications: Master's Degree in Social Work, Counseling or related field Five (5) or more years of relevant counseling experience, with at least 3 years being post-licensure Licensed Master Social Worker (LMSW) or Licensed Mental Health Counselor (LMHC) in the state of New York Applicants from other states or those who are license eligible must be licensed at the time of employment Applicants must meet stated minimum education and experience requirements. Preferred Qualifications: Clinical experience with young adult/adolescent populations Clinical work experience in a higher education setting Experience with electronic health record systems Clinical experience with at least one of traditionally underserved student population and/or International students Demonstrated experience with the assessment and treatment of trauma-related concerns, including interpersonal, sexual, developmental, and complex trauma, within a short-term model Professional clinical experience specifically treating eating disorder diagnoses Minimum Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Knowledge of crisis intervention techniques Ability to observe, assess, and record symptoms, reactions, and progress Ability to work effectively with a wide range of constituencies in a diverse community Ability to effectively communicate in written and verbal form Ability to effectively communicate information, test results, diagnoses and/or proposed treatment in a manner easily understood by the individuals Ability to assess mental status in patients and to provide treatment options Preferred Knowledge, Skill, and Abilities: Certified Clinical Trauma Professional (CCTP) Representative Job Duties: Counsel individuals or groups to help them understand problems, define goals, and develop realistic action plans Collect information about individuals or clients, using interviews, case histories, observational techniques, and other assessment methods for use in diagnosis and treatment planning. Develop therapeutic and treatment plans based on clients' interests, abilities, and needs Analyze data such as interview notes, test results, and reference manuals to identify symptoms and to diagnose the nature of clients' problems. Advise Clients on how counseling can help their state/condition Evaluate the results of counseling methods to determine the reliability and validity of treatments. Consult with other professionals to discuss therapies, treatments, counseling resources, or techniques, and to share occupational information Refer clients to specialists for non-counseling treatment of problems Provide consultation to teachers, administrators, and other staff as needed in responding to students who present with adjustment and mental health problems Some occasional after-hours work is required, including rotating on-call crisis counseling/consultation and as-needed student-mental health programming Complete and maintain records and reports regarding the students’ histories, progress, services provided, and other relevant information Promote mental health by participating in campus-wide outreach activities as necessary Other duties as needed Shift: Business Hours with weekends or evenings occasionally required Travel: Local travel between campus locations only Driving: Incidental driving possible, but not required Starting Salary/Rate: Expected hiring range: $62,250 - $66,400 / yr (10-months) NOTE: This is a 10-month role with a scheduled work period of August 1 through May 31 of the following year. The position will enter the non-work period beginning June 1, extending through July 31. This role is eligible for year-round benefits. Pay transparency disclosure: The selected candidate’s salary will be determined based on factors that include the available budget, internal equity, and the final candidate’s qualifications, experience, education and other job-related credentials. This hiring range is provided as Rensselaer’s good faith estimate of the expected hiring range at the time of posting. Application instructions: Follow the on-screen prompts to create a brief online profile. Please be ready to upload your resume and cover letter. If you need assistance with the online application process, please contact careers@rpi.edu. Job Posted Date: Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Total Compensation and Benefits Information: Rensselaer’s Total Compensation Program is designed to provide stable pay growth, a comprehensive and affordable benefits package, and a comprehensive and affordable retiree medical and prescription plan. Our goal is to provide you and your family with a comprehensive health and welfare program as an umbrella of financial security and protection during your employment. For more information, please visit Benefits | Human Resources (rpi.edu) . Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute is committed to the cultivation of a community that is welcoming, inclusive, and above all values learning. We welcome candidates who bring a variety of perspectives to Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute's work and campus communities. Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation or gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or other characteristic protected by law. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 74bc4471 Last Name (required) ffd538bf Email (required) d2d2ecf7 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Custodial Worker - Environmental Specialist Troy, NY Environmental & Site Services The Department of Environmental Services seeks applicants to fill its opening for several Cleaner openings. Public Safety Officer I Troy, NY Public Safety Office Entry level Public Safety opportunities available for service minded individuals interested in facilitating a safe and secure environment for the students, faculty, and staff who live, learn and work at Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute. Sergeant Troy, NY Public Safety Office The Public Safety Sergeant provides supervision of shift including responsibility for assigning and coordinating Officer duties, evaluation of daily patrol activity and reports, productivity reports, special events, conflict resolution, emergency response and law enforcement coordination. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 79da5446 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories CFHE Health Services Staff CFHE Health Services Staff Employment Type Full Time Full Time Locations Troy, NY, New York, United States Troy, NY, New York, United States First Name (required) 0598807d Last Name (required) 5e8ad964 Email (required) cd91a210 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
