    "https://careers.rpi.edu/jobs/endowed-chair-and-professor-of-finance-troy-ny-new-york-united-states": {
      "title": "Endowed Chair and Professor of Finance",
      "description": "Endowed Chair and Professor of Finance - Troy, NY, New York, United States Endowed Chair and Professor of Finance - Troy, NY, New York, United States Kiosk mode Endowed Chair and Professor of Finance Troy, NY Faculty Lally School of Management Full Time Add to favorites View favorites Job Summary: The Lally School of Management at Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute seeks applicants for the Kay & Jackson Tai ’72 Endowed Chair and Professor of Finance position starting Fall 2027, at the Full Professor level. The ideal candidate will work in interdisciplinary areas at the cutting edge of finance and analytics with a focus on risk management, quantitative methods, and the applications and implications of cybersecurity, artificial intelligence (AI), and quantum computing in finance. Candidates with a strong track record of conducting impactful research and innovative teaching in one or more of these areas are preferred. Who we are: Founded in 1824, Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute (RPI) is the first technological research university in the United States. We bring creativity, science, and technology together to address society's greatest challenges. We cultivate exceptional problem-solvers by immersing them in a culture of rigorous inquiry, disciplined practice, and hands-on application. Our strategic plan, RPI Forward, charts a pioneering course for the next era of RPI. Explore the RPI Forward plan. ↗︎ Nestled on a beautiful 275-acre campus in upstate NY, RPI is home to five schools, 32 research centers, three makerspaces, an observatory, one of the world’s fastest supercomputers, and the IBM Quantum System One - the first university-based quantum computer in the world. With top notch employee health and retirement benefits, Rensselaer offers its full-time employees a generous paid time off program, tuition remission, and opportunities for career growth. Minimum Qualifications: PhD degree in a relevant business discipline from an accredited university. Strong track record of producing original and innovative scholarly work. Publications in premier finance journals. Demonstrated record of effective teaching in graduate and undergraduate finance courses. Demonstrated commitment to teaching basic and advanced topics in finance, risk analytics, and emerging financial technologies. Demonstrated ability to contribute through service to the Lally School of Management and Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute. Preferred Qualifications: Research expertise in one or more of the following areas: risk management, analytics, AI and machine learning in finance, quantitative asset management, cybersecurity, quantum computing, or financial technology compliance and regulation. Experience teaching or developing courses in cybersecurity in financial services, AI and machine learning applications in finance, or quantum computing for financial analysis and decision-making. Experience in and deep knowledge of the financial services industry, including cybersecurity, AI adoption, or emerging quantum applications. Experience with interdisciplinary research and collaboration. Demonstrated interest in experiential learning and engagement with students through initiatives such as the Rensselaer Finance Club and student-managed James Fund. Minimum Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Knowledge of finance, quantitative methods, and emerging financial technologies. Knowledge of current research and developments in finance and risk analytics. Ability to conduct impactful, original, and innovative scholarly research. Ability to effectively teach undergraduate and graduate students. Ability to develop and teach courses in finance and emerging financial technologies. Ability to contribute effectively to an interdisciplinary academic community. Strong written and oral communication skills. Ability to collaborate effectively with faculty, students, and academic and professional colleagues. Preferred Knowledge, Skill, and Abilities: Knowledge of cybersecurity applications and implications within financial services. Knowledge of AI and machine learning applications in finance. Knowledge of quantum computing applications in financial analysis and decision-making. Knowledge of responsible generative AI, model risk, and explainability. Knowledge of quantum-resistant cryptography and its implications for financial services. Knowledge of fraud detection, operational resilience, financial data protection, and payment systems. Ability to engage students in experiential and applied learning. Representative Job Duties: Conduct original and innovative research in finance and related interdisciplinary areas. Publish scholarly research in premier finance journals and other appropriate academic outlets. Teach undergraduate and graduate courses in finance, risk analytics, and emerging financial technologies. Develop and teach courses supporting the B.S. in Finance, Markets, and Emerging Technologies and M.S. in Quantitative Finance and Risk Analytics programs. Advise and mentor undergraduate and graduate students. Contribute to interdisciplinary research and teaching initiatives. Engage with the Rensselaer Finance Club and student-managed James Fund. Utilize RPI's IBM Quantum System One, IBM Premium Quantum Cloud resources, and QED resources as appropriate for research and experiential learning. Provide service to the Lally School of Management and Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute. Participate in the broader academic and professional community through appropriate scholarly, teaching, and service activities. Shift: Business Hours: Monday - Friday Travel: As required for professional and academic activities. Local travel between campus locations only Driving: Incidental driving possible, but not required Starting Salary/Rate: Expected hiring range: $275,000 - $300,000 Pay transparency disclosure: The selected candidate’s salary will be determined based on factors that include the available budget, internal equity, and the final candidate’s qualifications, experience, education and other job-related credentials. This hiring range is provided as Rensselaer’s good faith estimate of the expected hiring range at the time of posting. Application instructions: Follow the on-screen prompts to create a brief online profile. Please be ready to upload your resume and cover letter. If you need assistance with the online application process, please contact careers@rpi.edu. Job Posted Date: Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Total Compensation and Benefits Information: Rensselaer’s Total Compensation Program is designed to provide stable pay growth, a comprehensive and affordable benefits package, and a comprehensive and affordable retiree medical and prescription plan. Our goal is to provide you and your family with a comprehensive health and welfare program as an umbrella of financial security and protection during your employment. For more information, please visit Benefits | Human Resources (rpi.edu) . Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute is committed to the cultivation of a community that is welcoming, inclusive, and above all values learning. We welcome candidates who bring a variety of perspectives to Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute's work and campus communities. Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation or gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or other characteristic protected by law. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 6cc939c3 Last Name (required) bf4d8cc2 Email (required) 238a468c Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Field House Temp Staff Troy, NY Field House Incumbents are hired on an if/when needed basis during events at the Houston Field House. Representative assignments include: Parking Lot Attendant, Usher, Zamboni Driver, Box Office Clerk, Ticket Taker, and Sound Technician. Custodial Worker - Environmental Specialist Troy, NY Environmental & Site Services The Department of Environmental Services seeks applicants to fill its opening for several Cleaner openings. Public Safety Officer I Troy, NY Public Safety Office Entry level Public Safety opportunities available for service minded individuals interested in facilitating a safe and secure environment for the students, faculty, and staff who live, learn and work at Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert d611c2c8 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty Lally School of Management Faculty Lally School of Management Employment Type Full Time Full Time Locations Troy, NY, New York, United States Troy, NY, New York, United States First Name (required) 25869725 Last Name (required) ac43d413 Email (required) 0aaef9bb Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
