    "https://careers.rpi.edu/jobs/microelectronics-researchers-troy-ny-new-york-united-states-68de7c94-4d82-43c0-b9c5-8be8ac3136ff": {
      "title": "Microelectronics Researchers",
      "description": "Microelectronics Researchers - Troy, NY, New York, United States Microelectronics Researchers - Troy, NY, New York, United States Kiosk mode Microelectronics Researchers Troy, NY Research: Microelectronics Researchers and Research Support Full Time Part Time Seasonal or Temporary Add to favorites View favorites Who we are Why Rensselaer? Join Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute's dynamic global community of changemaker including some of the world’s leading researchers, students, alumni, and faculty who ask the important questions and devise the scientific and technological innovations that make the world a better place for all of humanity. Nestled on a beautiful 275-acre campus in upstate NY, Rensselaer is home to five schools, 32 research centers, three makerspaces, an observatory, one of the world’s fastest supercomputers, and IBM's Quantum System One - the first university-based quantum computer in the world. Over the past decade, the research portfolio at Rensselaer has been completely transformed. As a top-tier technological research university, Rensselaer has invested in strategic partnerships, talented researchers, and sophisticated research platforms to address the most pressing global challenges of the 21st century. Today, the Rensselaer research enterprise comprises $104 million in annual research expenditures, supports a diverse range of research centers and platforms , and ensures the advancement of interdisciplinary research in six key areas: Life Science & Biotechnology (Bioscience, Bio Manufacturing, Bioscience, Diagnosis) Future Computing (Data / AI, High Performance Computing, Quantum, Bits/Neurons/Qubits) Energy, Environment, and Sustainability (Energy Solutions, Built Environment, Freshwater, Sustainability) Materials & Manufacturing (Mat. Discovery, Mat. Processing, Advanced Manufacturing, Robotics) Microelectronics (Mat. & Metrology, Hardware Co-design, Computational Microelectronics, Hetero-integration) Fundamental Knowledge (AstroX, Origins, Cognitive & Social, Financial) Microelectronics has played a significant role in nearly every major technological development of the last half-century. In keeping with our creative, interdisciplinary reputation for innovation, Rensselaer researchers cover the whole semiconductor spectrum, from theory to practice to product and from bench to bedside, across materials, design, devices, and systems. Please visit chips.rpi.edu for more information. The Office for Research collaborates with important external partners in the federal and state government, foundations and in industry to expand the impact our work and to support our world-class researchers as they improve lives, advance society, and change the world. Rensselaer faculty and alumni include more than 145 National Academy members, six members of the National Inventors Hall of Fame, six National Medal of Technology winners, five National Medal of Science winners, # astronauts, and a Nobel Prize winner in Physics. With nearly 200 years of experience advancing scientific and technological knowledge, Rensselaer remains focused on addressing global challenges with a spirit of ingenuity and collaboration. To learn more, please visit www.rpi.edu . Are you ready to change the world? Apply now! Job summary Some of the areas that may be hiring researchers and research support positions in the area of Microelectronics include: Materials & Metrology Hardware Co-design Computational Microelectronics Hetero-integration Note: The availability of positions is dependent on the availability of sponsored funding. Not all areas will have all positions, and some areas may be fully staffed. Qualifications Postdoctoral Research Associate - Candidates must have finished all requirements for their PhD or foreign equivalent at the beginning of their appointment Research Associate or (Sr.) Research Scientist - Opportunities exist for those with a relevant advanced degree, publication record, and/or significant additional years of paid professional experience in a related position. Individuals who possess these qualifications and who have the potential to, or a demonstrated track record of being able to build collaborative external partnerships are especially desirable (Sr.) Research Specialist - Positions require a relevant bachelor's degree / foreign equivalent or higher (Sr.) Research Engineer - Research Assistant - candidates must possess an associate's degree / foreign equivalent or relevant combination of experience, education and training Pay transparency Pay transparency disclosure: The actual salary/wage that is provided to selected candidates will be determined based on factors that include the available budget, internal equity, and the needs of the department, and the final candidate’s qualifications, experience, education, and other job-related credentials. The following hiring ranges are provided as Rensselaer’s good faith estimate of the expected hiring range at the time of posting. Postdoctoral Research Associate: $62,354 - $65,000 / yr Research Associate: $64,000 - $66,000 / yr Research Scientist: $66,000 - $95,000 / yr Sr. Research Scientist: $80,000 - $138,000 / yr *** Research Specialist: $18.00 - $26.44 / hr Sr. Research Specialist: $62,354 - 66,000 / yr *** Research Engineer: $66,000 - $86,000 / yr Sr. Research Engineer: $87,000 – $95,000 / yr *** Research Assistant: $16.00 - $22.00 / hr Application instructions Follow the on-screen prompts to create an application. Please be ready to upload any required documents, such as your resume and cover letter If you need assistance with the online application process, please contact careers@rpi.edu Job posted date Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Total Compensation and Benefits Information Rensselaer’s Total Compensation Program is designed to provide stable pay growth, a comprehensive and affordable benefits package, and a comprehensive and affordable retiree medical and prescription plan. Rensselaer is recognized locally and nationally for the depth and breadth of its compensation and benefits program. Our goal is to provide you and your family with a comprehensive health and welfare program as an umbrella of financial security and protection during your employment. For more information, please visit Benefits | Human Resources (rpi.edu) . Rensselaer is committed to the cultivation of a community that is welcoming, inclusive, and above all values learning. We welcome candidates who bring a variety of perspectives to Rensselaer’s work and campus communities. Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation or gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or other characteristic protected by law. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 4dfbada9 Last Name (required) 128a82a5 Email (required) 49e7a31d Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Field House Temp Staff Troy, NY Field House Incumbents are hired on an if/when needed basis during events at the Houston Field House. Representative assignments include: Parking Lot Attendant, Usher, Zamboni Driver, Box Office Clerk, Ticket Taker, and Sound Technician. Endowed Chair and Professor of Finance Troy, NY Management Academics The Lally School of Management at Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute seeks applicants for the Kay & Jackson Tai ’72 Senior Chair position starting Fall 2027, at the Full Professor level. The ideal candidate will work in interdisciplinary areas at the cutting edge of finance and analytics with a focus on risk management, quantitative methods, and the applications and implications of cybersecurity, artificial intelligence (AI), and quantum computing in finance. Candidates with a strong track record of conducting impactful research and innovative teaching in one or more of these areas are preferred. Custodial Worker - Environmental Specialist Troy, NY Environmental & Site Services The Department of Environmental Services seeks applicants to fill its opening for several Cleaner openings. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert ec4bb6c2 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Research: Microelectronics Researchers and Research Support Research: Microelectronics Researchers and Research Support Employment Type Full Time Part Time Seasonal or Temporary Full Time Part Time Seasonal or Temporary Locations Troy, NY, New York, United States Troy, NY, New York, United States First Name (required) 7ce68d01 Last Name (required) 8b03d1b2 Email (required) 7d166b22 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
    }
